  "text": "Noísiu and his brothers faced Concobar's warriors. His men killed them without a chance to defend themselves. Deirdre was carried back to the court in chains. There she charged the king with lying and cruelty. Concobar lost interest once he held her. To mock her further he gave her to one of her lover's killers. The man took Deirdre away in his chariot. She leapt from the vehicle and died when her head struck a stone. Many of Ulster's finest soldiers turned against Concobar because of this. They left his kingdom and served queen Medb of Connacht. Medb then opened the war that lies behind the Tain Bo Cuailnge.",
